    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0348" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00 Congress, Communist International, VII/54:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-19T19:00:00-04:00">August 19, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. Your 357, August 18, 3 p.m.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d253-f1"/> In view of
                    departure of the President shortly from Washington, perhaps at end of present
                    week <pb facs="0349" n="243" xml:id="pg243"/> Department would like to have your
                    recommendations and suggestions immediately upon close of Congress, by Wednesday
                    the 21st if possible. In view of information which you have already forwarded,
                    Department doubts that speeches and resolutions of concluding sessions of the
                    Congress will be of material importance in connection with your consideration of
                    the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
